                                                    "desc:8":  "§6§lEVERY INLET SITS WHERE IT IS USED§r\nThere is no plumbing wall. Each insert and extract point is cut into the building it feeds, on the exact course it enters the plant\u0027s logic: rods go in at the fuel course they burn on, water at the drum, coolant and propellant at the chamber that spends them, power at the generator.\n\n[img height=480]btsquests:textures/gui/point-of-use.png[/img]\n\n§e§lTHE SILO FACE - the flat wall your controller is set into§r\nThree courses, one cell either side of the controller\u0027s own column - exactly as drawn above:\n  §by2§r  §bROD§r Input Bus . §bDEP§r Depleted Output Bus\n     §8the bottom FUEL course - the exact segment the cascade burns§r\n  §by1§r  §bH2O§r Input Hatch . §bSILO CONTROL BLOCK§r . §bOUT§r Output Hatch\n     §8the drum course - feedwater in, waste water and exported steam out§r\n  §by0§r  §bMAINT§r Maintenance Hatch, in the cell beside the controller\n\n§e§lTHE SPIRAL CHAMBER FRONT WALL - one course above the floor§r\n  §bCOOL§r Input Hatch - coolant, for the thing that actually overheats\n  §bPROP§r Input Hatch - bulk propellant, directly under the eight injectors it stocks\n  §bMNT§r Maintenance Hatch - the chamber carries its own, in the floor\u0027s front-right corner\n\n§8The output manifold\u0027s own sockets - dynamos, energy and lasers - are step 9.§r\n\n§e§lDO THIS§r\nBreak the plain casing in each socket cell and place the machine there. Then run your logistics to each one; nothing is shared and nothing travels down a pipe you have to build.\n\n§a§lDONE WHEN§r\nAll §bnine§r machines listed above are in your inventory at the same time.\n§8This quest only LOOKS at what you are carrying, and it takes nothing. Hold the whole set at once, CLAIM it, and only then break the casings and set the machines into the wall. Already installed them? Wrench them back out for a moment - the check is on your inventory, not on the building.§r\n\n§e§lCHECK YOUR WORK§r\nRight-click the §bSilo Control Block§r you just set into the face. It prints the whole instrument panel, and the REACTOR group carries a §bSupply§r line reading §20 rods queued -\u003e 0 pillar gaps§r.\n§8Both zeros are right. A pillar gap is an empty segment in a §bReactor Fuel Pillar Frame§r, and not one of those is standing yet. What this step pays you is §b16 fuel-column BLOCKS§r - one block is one segment and 8 of them make a pillar, so that is §b2 pillars§r - and they go up in step 5. Gaps appear when you raise the pillars; the queue moves when you feed the bus.§r\n§6This is the step where the plant FORMS for the first time.§r §8Maintenance, Feedwater Input, Output Hatch and Depleted Output Bus are the only four sockets the structure actually demands, and they all just went in. Everything you fit from here on is added to a plant that is already alive.§r\n\n[note]You never touch a rod port inside the silo again. The controller distributes rods from that one bus to all 45-201 pillars itself, every decay cycle - best grade first, lowest empty segment first.[/note]",
